            <ArticleTitle>[Diseases of the small intestine from the surgical aspect (author's transl)].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>1165-8</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Among 37,857 operations in a general surgical department (1965-1975), 205 interventions on the small intestine were necessary- enterotomies, oversuturing, amputations and resections. The operations are evaluated with regard to etiology, clinical aspects and operative technique.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
